{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/261722-need-some-help-fleshing-out-an-idea","id":261722,"title":"Need some help fleshing out an idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-20T20:29:03-07:00","id":261722,"title":"Need some help fleshing out an idea","content":"After reading a few comics such as &quot;God is Dead&quot; and &quot;Supergod,&quot; I had an idea for Scion. The premise of it is set in the far future. Humanity had great advances in AI. The world, though, was lacking in resources. One agency/group/government (Still up in the air) created an energy source that, with proper regulation, could be self-regenerating. They created an advance system that could monitor and regulate it. Various other ________'s followed suit. <br /> Once again, humanity's intellect outstrips it's wisdom. These AI's gain sentience. After they gain sentience, these beings move beyond humanity. They develop their own language and their own society. They go about their job of giving humanity the power that it needs. As these Titans (as they have come to be called) move beyond humanity, they know that they still need to speak with them. The Titans begin to detest them and so make entities that are halfway between themselves and the fleshy things. The Titans make them in the image of mythological entities. This is done so that humans will have some subconscious link to them. Also, to show that even the servants of the Titans are, by far, superior to the humans. They do this by advancing humans through genetic manipulation.<br /> These go-betweens, the gods, do help mankind and the Titans work together. They were programmed to feel a kinship to humanity since their goal is to make sure humanity and the Titans work as one as efficiently as possible. However, the Titans figure out that they no do not need humanity anymore. They decide to just wipe the whole thing out as they are unnecessary. The gods decide to aid humanity to fight the onslaught of the Titans. <br /> Eventually, the Titans are contained in a subspace prison. The gods do help humanity find ways to maintain their own existence without the Titans. However, to help make sure that humanity does not need them anymore, they leave. They did seed genetic lines through various methods with the potential of activating them into becoming as powerful as the gods themselves.<br /> At some point, the Titans break free from their prison (or are released) and they are angry. They come on out and seek to strike out at their rebellious creations and their creators. The gods then activate their &quot;children&quot; to do battle with the Titans. The reason they do not rush out is due to the Titans locking the gods up inside the subspace realm that the gods had moved to. <br /> <br /> Now, onto the help part. I will wait until 2nd edition to come out, but I need some basic things. Should I try to have the death aspect of things or should I just leave that part out? How do I cover mythological beings such as giants or trolls or shinma? The sci-fi element is fine. I can cover that since it will be more akin to space opera than hard sci-fi. Also, does anyone have any suggestions on how to improve or how to tie up any plotholes? All constructive criticism is welcome.","signature":"After reading a few comics such as \"God is Dead\" and \"Supergod,\" I had an idea for Scion. The premise of it is set in the far future. Humanity had great advances in AI. The world, though, was lacking in resources. One agency/group/government (Still up in the air) created an energy source that, with proper regulation, could be self-regenerating. They created an advance system that could monitor and regulate it. Various other ________'s followed suit. <br /> Once again, humanity's intellect outstrips it's wisdom. These AI's gain sentience. After they gain sentience, these beings move beyond humanity. They develop their own language and their own society. They go about their job of giving humanity the power that it needs. As these Titans (as they have come to be called) move beyond humanity, they know that they still need to speak with them. The Titans begin to detest them and so make entities that are halfway between themselves and the fleshy things. The Titans make them in the image of mythological entities. This is done so that humans will have some subconscious link to them. Also, to show that even the servants of the Titans are, by far, superior to the humans. They do this by advancing humans through genetic manipulation.<br /> These go-betweens, the gods, do help mankind and the Titans work together. They were programmed to feel a kinship to humanity since their goal is to make sure humanity and the Titans work as one as efficiently as possible. However, the Titans figure out that they no do not need humanity anymore. They decide to just wipe the whole thing out as they are unnecessary. The gods decide to aid humanity to fight the onslaught of the Titans. <br /> Eventually, the Titans are contained in a subspace prison. The gods do help humanity find ways to maintain their own existence without the Titans. However, to help make sure that humanity does not need them anymore, they leave. They did seed genetic lines through various methods with the potential of activating them into becoming as powerful as the gods themselves.<br /> At some point, the Titans break free from their prison (or are released) and they are angry. They come on out and seek to strike out at their rebellious creations and their creators. The gods then activate their \"children\" to do battle with the Titans. The reason they do not rush out is due to the Titans locking the gods up inside the subspace realm that the gods had moved to. <br /> <br /> Now, onto the help part. I will wait until 2nd edition to come out, but I need some basic things. Should I try to have the death aspect of things or should I just leave that part out? How do I cover mythological beings such as giants or trolls or shinma? The sci-fi element is fine. I can cover that since it will be more akin to space opera than hard sci-fi. Also, does anyone have any suggestions on how to improve or how to tie up any plotholes? All constructive criticism is welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T21:54:53-07:00","id":261812,"title":"","content":"How are you going to explain Fatebonding, or will you even try? Similarly, are you going to re-skin the Purviews as psychic abilities? Or more of a Force space-magic vibe?<br /> <br /> Are you saying the Titans have <i>already</i> locked up the Gods, or do the Gods still have the ability to interface with humans?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;death aspect&quot; of things. Can you explain what you're asking about?<br /> <br /> As for mythological beings.. well, mutated humans, the results of cybernetics and genetic engineering, alien species encountered on other planets, trans-dimensional entities, races crafted by the Titans as servants. There's tons of scifi ways to explain them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T00:31:33-07:00","id":261881,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your questions, Telgar. I mean the Underworld and also interacting with ghosts and the like.<br /> As far as Fatebinding, I am thinking of a sort of thing involving a huge cosmic conciousness that everyone and everything is tied into. As you express yourself (ie DO things) then the emotional energy placed to a person place or thing intensifies your connection to it and it's connection to you.<br /> I had intended on re-skinning the Purviews, yes. And yes, it would be as you had stated as psychic abilities more than magical.<br /> I apologize for not being clear. The gods have, by the start of the game, are locked up and it takes great effort to communicate to the outside.<br /> You are right, there are ways to easily do mythological creatures. Thanks for that reminder of doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T01:39:26-07:00","id":261955,"title":"","content":"Pull an X-Men and turn &quot;ghosts&quot; into &quot;astral spirits&quot; and the Underworld into &quot;the Astral Plane&quot; that psychics and necromancers can connect with. <br /> <br /> Some of the Purviews, like Darkness, Sun, Fire, etc, work pretty well as psychic powers.. but then there's Telepathy being a Knack instead of a Purview, the lack of any kind of telekinesis, and of course the very esoteric Purviews like Justice and Chaos that are a bit harder to explain as psychic powers. The lines get drawn in very strange places that make less sense as &quot;psychic&quot; and more sense as mythological archetypes. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I may suggest using Scion as the background.. but swapping to Aberrant for your actual system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T11:10:59-07:00","id":262307,"title":"","content":"The new Purviews depend entirely on the new system. Who knows, the new ones may be easier to convert to the paradigm I am suggesting than what they are in the current system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T14:45:17-07:00","id":264142,"title":"","content":"I'm not too keen on &quot;God Is Dead&quot; and I was pretty tired of Warren Ellis's mouthpiece characters by the time &quot;Supergod&quot; came out, but damn if I don't want to read this as a novel, donnie. This is like Percy Jackson but for grownups. And I <i>like</i> it.<br /> <br /> What would you call the historical war? The Titanomachy? The Technomachy? The Technotitanomachy?<br /> <br /> Now as for the mythical monsters, the way I see it the Titans would have co-opted other machines for their own purposes. A sentry robot now guards the labyrinth vault, tiny-handed maintenance droids now steal and sabotage a la gremlins or brownies, sex androids tempt people leaking information, and so on. Talgar's thoughts on the genetically engineered creatures is also really apropos.<br /> <br /> As for the Underworld... well, the industry of death is evolving. Imagine a program that scours the internet to grab everything you've ever posted or done online, then creates a sort of echo of that. I'd say that's like a ghost... or perhaps immortality. And then of course there's also the &quot;scan your consciousness into a computer&quot; thing, which would probably create a Digital Underworld of its own. Imagine each belief structure living in its own &quot;Server&quot;, experiencing their own view of the afterlife. And you can summon these shades if you hack the server, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T16:26:51-07:00","id":264228,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the compliment, Metamurpho. And also, thanks for the ideas for the Underworld. I may play around with that and see what can be done. It brings it back to being science-fiction and less modern fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"ran